message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Homological Cascade Engine"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/homological-cascade-engine"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  Experimental research software for chain-complex diffusion, Hodge
  decomposition, robust MAD telemetry scoring, and streaming
  Peaks-Over-Threshold thresholds. v0.6.0 adds a classical, synthetic
  co-exact residual-energy scorer with QKD-motivated names; it is not a QKD
  system or adaptive-optics hardware, gives no security guarantee, and does
  not detect real eavesdroppers. All reported results are synthetic.
keywords:
  - research software
  - chain complex
  - Hodge decomposition
  - anomaly detection
  - extreme value theory
  - synthetic data
license: MIT
version: "0.6.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
